# Commit messages

Use `type(scope): summary` to match repository history. Only commit when asked.
Do not create a commit until `pnpm format:check` and `pnpm lint` have been run
against the to-be-committed tree and passed. Also run `pnpm compile` and the
affected unit tests when types or behavior changed. These are CI gates.

- **type:** `feat`, `fix`, `test`, or `chore`
- **scope:** the area that changed (`extension`, `e2e`, `unit`, `ci`, `package`, `tooling`)
- **summary:** imperative, lowercase after the colon, no trailing period
- **body:** optional `-` bullets only when they add why the subject does not cover
- **trailers:** never add Cursor, Copilot, or other AI `Co-authored-by`, `Made-with`, or `Generated-by` lines

```text
❌ BAD
Fixed the HMR crash.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

✅ GOOD
fix(extension): add empty matches so WXT HMR does not crash

- Leave matches empty so optional host permissions stay optional
```

After `git commit` or `git commit --amend`, check `git log -1 --format='%B'`
and rewrite HEAD if a wrapper left a forbidden trailer in history.
